# DarwinTV

Read `AGENTS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/hardware/pi5.md` and `docs/boot-flow.md`.

- No Apple firmware, IPSW, kernelcache, device tree, userland or keys in the repository.
- No activation/DRM circumvention.
- Do not invent hardware addresses; cite the DTS or `docs/hardware/pi5.md`.
- Kernel changes go in `patches/`, one logical change per patch.
- Run `make check` and `make loader BOARD=pi5` before proposing changes.
- QEMU before hardware; never run destructive commands on a real Pi.
- Conventional Commits + DCO sign-off.
